]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/F1\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"duplicate_of\":\"circuit/F1-sheet-file-case-mismatch\",\"reason\":\"Same defect as circuit/F1-sheet-file-case-mismatch: identical condition (sheet filename case mismatch breaking ERC/netlist), identical mechanism (VR-conditioner section invisible to native verification), and identical evidence set (15 extra_footprint parity items, U10 MAX9924 geometry, console parity count). Content fully subsumed by the accepted canonical finding.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"schematic_parity: 15x type=extra_footprint (C25 uuid 0070999b, U10 uuid 4ccdf03c, et al.)\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"footprint U10 value MAX9924 at (133.811, 56.081)\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"circuit/F2-drc-error-violations\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"duplicate_of\":\"check/drc\",\"reason\":\"Restates the same native DRC run that check/drc reports: the 13 error-severity violations (5 padstack, 5 annular_width, 3 starved_thermal) are a subset of the 142 violations counted by the accepted check finding, from the identical tool invocation and board sha. The analysis is correct and supported (console count plus check by_severity/by_type breakdown), so it is linked to the accepted canonical check rather than dismissed. The individual error items lie beyond the 100000-byte drc.json prefix and should be localized from the full report during repair.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/console.log\",\"locator\":\"line 1: 'Found 142 violations'\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"check details by_severity error=13; by_type padstack=5, annular_width=5, starved_thermal=3 (items beyond included prefix)\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/execution.json\",\"locator\":\"argv '--severity-all'; exit_code 0; same board as check/drc\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/F2\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"duplicate_of\":\"check/drc\",\"reason\":\"Identical to circuit/F2-drc-error-violations and a subset of the accepted check/drc: same 13 error-severity violations (padstack 5, annular_width 5, starved_thermal 3) from the same kicad-cli run on the same saved board. Mechanism description (drill breakout, inconsistent padstacks, starved thermal reliefs) is sound but adds no separate defect beyond the failing DRC check it restates.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/console.log\",\"locator\":\"line 1: 'Found 142 violations'\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"check details by_severity error=13; by_type padstack=5, annular_width=5, starved_thermal=3\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"circuit/F3-can2-termination-dnp\",\"disposition\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"Condition verified in the native schematic: R36 (value 120, dnp yes, in_bom no, 'n.p.' text annotation) wires through (119.38,86.36)->(121.92,88.9) to the CAN2- rail and through (111.76,86.36)->(109.22,83.82) to the CAN2+ rail, so the only differential termination on the internal wideband bus is unpopulated in both sheet instances (refs R36 and R37, confirmed dnp in geometry dnp_refs with pad nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2-). The 47p caps C29/C30/C33/C34 are line-to-ground filters, not termination. Internal dual-wideband CAN termination is explicitly in the review scope and no populated termination is evidenced anywhere in the packet; correctly held at concern (not defect) because module- or harness-side termination cannot be excluded from supplied data. Canonical for this issue.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"symbol uuid d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543: R36 value 120, (dnp yes), (in_bom no), instances R36/R37; text 'n.p.' uuid 98ed307b at (113.03, 76.2); wires uuid ccecad78/e4425ab5/6140c09a/5371a59b tie pins to CAN2+ (y=83.82) and CAN2- (y=88.9)\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"dnp_refs includes R36, R37; footprint R36 dnp=true, pad 1 net /CAN2+, pad 2 net /CAN2- at (175.014, 142.129)\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/README.md\",\"locator\":\"'Dual wideband O2 sensor controllers ... (connected internally to CAN bus #2)'\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/F3\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"duplicate_of\":\"circuit/F3-can2-termination-dnp\",\"reason\":\"Same finding as circuit/F3-can2-termination-dnp: both DNP 120R terminations (R36/R37) across /CAN2+ and /CAN2- with intentional 'n.p.' annotation, same mechanism (unterminated bus reflections risking the internal wideband link), same concern-level framing conditional on unverifiable module/harness termination. Fully subsumed by the accepted canonical concern.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"symbol R36 uuid d69380f9: value 120, (dnp yes), (in_bom no); text 'n.p.' uuid 98ed307b\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"dnp_refs includes R36, R37; footprint R36 dnp=true spanning /CAN2+ to /CAN2-\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"circuit/F4-footprint-library-hygiene\",\"disposition\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"Verified verbatim in the included drc.json prefix: J2 footprint_symbol_mismatch ('Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)', uuid f447e585) plus lib_footprint_issues 'configuration does not include the footprint library Simon' on P1/P3/P5/P6/J1/J4, against a backdrop of 106 lib_footprint_mismatch warnings. No demonstrated electrical fault (DRC 0 unconnected items), so minor concern is the right calibration; retained as the canonical footprint/library hygiene finding covering both the J2 substitution and the library-drift population. Subsumes physical/F4 and physical/F5.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"schematic_parity: footprint_symbol_mismatch for Footprint J2 uuid f447e585-df78-4239-b8cb-4653b3837bb1 (Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD vs fome_modules:polygonus)\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"violations type=lib_footprint_issues ('Simon' library absent) for P1 uuid 1646febd, P3 uuid 6d6b5ea5, P5 uuid 91098c1d, P6 uuid 89385b4b, J1 uuid 93ba26da, J4 uuid a7443703; 106x type=lib_footprint_mismatch\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"circuit/F5-canrx-label-direction\",\"disposition\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"Verified by geometric trace of the native schematic: U20 (TJA1051T-3) is placed mirror-y at (166.37, 86.36), which puts RXD pin 4 (declared pin type output, symbol offset -12.7, +2.54) at (179.07, 83.82); wire uuid 327ec337 runs (179.07,83.82)-(204.47,83.82) to hierarchical label 'CAN_RX' declared (shape input). An output-driven sheet port declared as input is a real direction mismatch; CAN_TX->TXD (input pin) is correctly shaped, confirming only CAN_RX is wrong. No netlist impact, so info-level concern is correct; relevant because ERC (which would police this) cannot currently run per circuit/F1. Canonical; subsumes physical/F6.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"hierarchical_label 'CAN_RX' uuid 0cfcbd19 (shape input) at (204.47, 83.82); wire uuid 327ec337 (179.07,83.82)-(204.47,83.82); symbol U20 lib_id Interface_CAN_LIN:TJA1051T-3 at (166.37 86.36) (mirror y), lib pin RXD number 4 pin type output at (-12.7, 2.54)\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/F4\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"duplicate_of\":\"circuit/F4-footprint-library-hygiene\",\"reason\":\"The J2 footprint substitution (Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD vs symbol-declared fome_modules:polygonus, uuid f447e585) is the same parity item already carried by the accepted circuit/F4-footprint-library-hygiene, with the same minor-concern assessment and the same observation that the 'Simon' library is absent from configuration. No additional condition or mechanism beyond the canonical finding.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"schematic_parity: footprint_symbol_mismatch for Footprint J2 uuid f447e585-df78-4239-b8cb-4653b3837bb1\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/F5\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"duplicate_of\":\"circuit/F4-footprint-library-hygiene\